-check feature probe sui notebook perchè da gli stessi risultati in tutti i casi ✅
🔷In Attack B, the attacker uses a k-NN classifier on the embeddings.
If the code calls model.zero_sequence() for the "no-seed" scenario, it multiplies the backbone embedding h by 0 (m=h ⊙ s_k). This makes every single embedding an all-zero vector, regardless of the input image or the model used.
When you fit a k-NN on identical all-zero vectors, it will simply default to predicting the most frequent class or the first class it saw in the training set. If that class happens to belong to Task 3, it explains why you get a consistent 3.9% on Task 3 and 0.0% everywhere else across all models.

